{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he said to his daughters.</b> A father's father is called father, as in 'the Elohim of my father Abraham' (Genesis 31:42), and also 'Nebuchadnezzar your father' (Daniel 5:11). And a son's son is called son, and likewise the daughters [are called] 'daughters' and the sons [are called] 'sons' (Genesis 31:43), 'and you his son, Belshazzar' (Daniel 5:22)." "And he said. Scripture adopted a concise manner, for it did not mention 'and she called him,' because it is known from reason." "קִרֶאן לוֹ. A strange word, because nothing else is on its pattern."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:16.156483183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}